				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"></span><table width="90%" cellspacing="1" cellpadding="3" border="0" align="center"><tr> 	  <td><span class="genmed"><b>Quote:</b></span></td>	</tr>	<tr>	  <td class="quote">- Fixed a bug that caused a short delay in the hit point updates from healing spells</td>	</tr></table><span class="postbody">
<br />

<br />
Zantaer and I were talking about this after the failed dragon fight in HoH.
<br />

<br />
When he died, I saw "Zantaer died." this occurs with you either die from a dot, or when there is a delay between getting healed, and your client updating your health.  
<br />

<br />
The latter is this:
<br />

<br />
The server says, - a dragon hits Zantaer for 900, new hitpoints of Zantaer is 249. - Zantaer is healed for 7000, new hit points is 7249.  -a dragon hits Zantaer for 600, new hit points is 6649.
<br />

<br />
The client sees this - a dragon hits Zantaer for 900, new hitpoints of Zantaer is 249. - Zantaer is healed for 7000 will add the hps in a half a second.  -a dragon hits Zantaer for 600, new hit points is -351.  Player is dead, tell server player has died.  Cancel 7000 hp heal.
<br />

<br />
Server says, - Zataer dead?  hmm, can't be the health, player still has 6649 hps, but if you say he is dead, we beleive you.  I guess he just "died."
<br />

<br />
I am glad they fixed this.  I have died so many times after getting healed by Divine Arb and even using LoH on myself because of this.  I would see the message I had been healed for a large amount, but the HP total didn't go up and the next hit killed me.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
